WEBVTT

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.000
Oh, sorry.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.800
No, I wasn't paying attention either.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.540
Your bag...

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.650
I'm so sorry.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.520
Were there any eggs inside?

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.660
<b>It's okay.</b>

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.080
<b>There wasn't anything important inside.</b>

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.080
<b>Really, don't worry about it.</b>

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:56.850
<b>Bye.</b>

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.180
<b>Ah, please wait!</b>

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:00.830
You forgot this.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.290
Oh, thank you.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.060
So...

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.020
Do you like anpan?

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:13.890
<b>Meals Should Be Balanced</b>

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.640
I don't.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.260
Anpan and milk.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.980
This is how I run a stakeout.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.120
I don't eat anything else until it's over.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:29.570
Basically, it's an offering to the gods.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:32.910
I personally can't stand it, but the god of stakeouts is a big fan, so that's that.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:36.210
A truth that has been shown in police dramas around the world.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.430
For the success of this stakeout,

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.250
I must suppress my desire to eat curry, katsudon, and yakiniku,

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.700
and munch on anpan instead.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.370
You're not supposed to come into contact with the target.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.810
And you're supposed to be an inspector?

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:54.040
Do you realize how weird it is to stake out a stakeout?

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.890
You should have volunteered if you have nothing better to do.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.270
Don't get so upset.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:01.880
I see that you're only eating anpan again.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.020
You can be superstitious if you want,

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.630
but you won't last long if you aren't eating right.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.280
Sorry about the wait.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.020
Oh, thanks.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.660
Don't even bother, Vice Chief.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.820
I don't need ramen!

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.250
Well, if you insist, I suppose I don't have a choice.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.280
An order from you is absolute.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.510
Huh? What'd you say?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.890
Nothing.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:29.220
So how would you describe this Sachi Narasaki?

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.340
She seems to be a nice person,

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.440
going by the five days I've been watching her.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.720
I find it hard to believe that she's the older sister of a brutal Joi terrorist.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.670
Oh?

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.000
If you look at Sogo,

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:44.980
one sibling tends to be more responsible when the other is anything but.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.810
Vice Chief, you're a little too close...

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.920
And what about Donbei?

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.010
He's been running around like crazy.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.330
Apparently, he stole money from his fellow terrorists.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.340
They're trying to chase him down.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.850
His only option is to run to his sister.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:05.770
I can't say that I like the idea of using his sister as bait.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:10.010
Do you like the idea of letting her brother run wild?

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:16.630
Besides, what if the Joi who are chasing Donbei decide to use her as bait...

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.020
We'll use his sister as bait to wipe them all out.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.050
Leave the dirty work to us.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:27.980
Yamazaki, I'm giving you a different mission.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:29.990
Protect the girl.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.610
Sagaru Yamazaki's Observation Report:

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:36.200
<b>Week 1 of Living on Anpan</b>

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.870
I've been living on anpan for an entire week now.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.660
What I'd give for a bowl of miso soup.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.770
The girl hasn't made a move yet.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.970
Sachi Narasaki.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.740
Owner of the bar Nonbei.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.230
The story is that she's a dutiful daughter

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.930
who's been running her father's business by herself since he died four years ago.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:57.460
On the other hand, her brother Donbei is notorious for being a nasty villain.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:02.010
He regularly came to his sister for money after she took over the bar.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.430
A dutiful daughter under duress,

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:07.280
the younger brother who continues to put her in danger,

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.380
and the terrorists who are after them.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:14.240
My mission is to monitor the Joi terrorists,

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:15.990
while protecting the girl.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:19.990
I, Sagaru Yamazaki, Shinsengumi inspector, vow to protect her!

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:23.670
And with my newfound determination, I once again munch on anpan.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.150
Day 8 of living on anpan.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.540
When I went to the supermarket yesterday,

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:32.650
I could hear people whispering, "Anpanman is here! No kidding!" in the back,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.880
<b>Nonbei</b>

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.930
but the girl hasn't made a move yet.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.390
Her customers are all regulars.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.800
Every day is the same.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.690
I can only hope that her peaceful life lasts forever.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.030
As I begin to forget my purpose here,

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.340
I once again munch on anpan.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.020
Day 12 of living on anpan.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.470
I've just realized that it's been days since I've talked to anyone.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:58.910
The last words I spoke were, "No, put it in one bag," three days ago,

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.720
but the girl hasn't made a move yet.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.160
For a moment, I almost thought that she was looking at me,

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:06.540
<b>Nonbei</b>

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:06.870
but it must have been my imagination.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.860
As I try to pull myself together,

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.750
I once again munch on anpan.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.850
But I could only finish half of it.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.060
Day 15 of living on anpan.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.570
When I went to the convenience store,

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:18.090
people started whispering, "The one-bag guy is here!"

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.260
"He's gonna buy anpan and milk!"

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.780
"In one bag!" and stuff,

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:27.430
<b>Nonbei</b>

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.340
but the girl hasn't made a move yet.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:28.240
What do I do if nothing happens?

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.770
As I attempt to ignore those doubts,

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:32.710
I once again munch on anpan.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.690
And then I throw it all up.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.990
Day 20 of living on anpan.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:41.160
It's been so long since I last spoke that I was wondering if my voice still worked,

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.610
so I screamed at the top of my lungs and the guy next door replied,

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:44.620
"Shut up!"

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.830
while banging on the wall, which had me jumping up and down with joy

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.510
over the fact that I actually held a conversation,

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.870
but the girl still hasn't made a move yet.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:54.630
She just smiles day after day.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:58.690
There are more exciting ways to live.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:02.330
Such as harboring a fugitive younger brother.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.270
And with that thought, I once again...

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.100
...smash anpan against the wall.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.350
Day 22 of living on anpan.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.170
Give me a break already.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:14.010
When is her younger brother going to show up?

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.880
When will I be released from this anpan curse?

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:17.840
Shut up!

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.140
Hurry, younger brother!

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:23.290
Save me from the endless anpan!

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.160
As I make a wish from the bottom of my heart,

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.080
I sparking the anpan into the sky!

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.250
Day 23 of living on anpan.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.580
I sparking the anpan into the supermarket clerk!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.000
Day 24 of living on anpan.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.590
I sparking the anpan into the convenience store clerk!

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.840
Day 25 of living on anpan.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.930
I sparking the anpan into the vice chief!

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:44.260
Day 28 of living on anpan.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:47.050
I wake up and discover that I have no memory of the past few days.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.580
However, despite all the change I've gone through,

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.410
the girl hasn't made a move yet.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.980
Like always, she scatters anpan on the road,

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.940
and puts the anpan above the entrance.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.530
And then at anpan-night,

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.980
she anpans the anpan and anpans.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:04.380
Anpanning the anpan to anpan the anpan and anpanny anpan, anpan, anpan...

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.200
<b>Day 30 of Living on Anpan</b>

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.710
<b>ANPAN</b>

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:17.400
Day 31 of living on anpan.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:23.090
When I woke up, I was standing in an unfamiliar place, covered in anko.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:26.970
Who gives a damn about the mission or girl?!

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:30.100
I refuse to take another bite of anpan!

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.070
I couldn't take it anymore.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.640
I no longer cared.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:37.230
I headed back to the room to pack up and leave.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.360
But there I found...

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.010
I didn't realize we were neighbors.

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:47.460
You'll ruin your health if you only eat anpan.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:50.950
Here are some leftover meat and potatoes if you don't mind.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:53.020
Thank you for watching over me.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:54.460
From Nonbei.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:59.130
The tears wouldn't stop...

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.620
I don't know when she realized I was watching her.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:05.090
I don't know how much she actually knew.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:07.180
One thing was clear...

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:10.700
I wasn't worthy of her gratitude.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:14.390
Since I was ready to abandon her because of my stupid superstition...

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:21.630
That day, I turned against the god of stakeouts.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.530
<b>Greater Edo Hospital</b>

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:26.420
Day 3 of meat and potatoes.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:28.030
I woke up...

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.170
...to find myself staring at an unfamiliar ceiling.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.650
And the vice chief with a disgusted look on his face.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:36.710
Vice Chief, where am I?

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.790
The hospital.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:38.400
Huh?

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.510
What happened to me?

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.460
What about Sachi-san? Her brother?

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:42.920
What happened to them?

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:44.430
They got away.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.390
What?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.760
They took the money and ran.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:49.280
Yamazaki...

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.940
We were tricked by the girl.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:56.500
The siblings were working together to steal money from the Joi.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:59.470
The sister noticed my presence immediately,

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:02.490
so she spent an entire month acting to fool me.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:05.460
And once I fell apart,

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.570
she used the pretense of kindness to poison me.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:11.180
Women are damn scary.

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:14.260
Hiding under layer after layer of makeup.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:17.210
Do we ever get a chance to see their real faces?

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.680
Well, she still served as the perfect bait.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:24.810
We rounded up all the ruffians who were trailing her.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.750
That more than makes up for the two who got away.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:32.130
We were able to freely move around because you were there.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.940
Sorry about the wait.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.880
Yamazaki, you did a good job.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:45.230
Vice Chief, this isn't like you.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:48.160
Are you trying to make me feel better?

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:50.440
It's not like I'm depressed or anything.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:54.610
I'm used to being fooled by women and failing missions.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:58.110
But I was hoping that...

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.460
...I could at least lose on my own terms.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.160
I guess that you aren't in the mood for ramen.

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:09.470
Can I ask for a favor?

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:12.690
It really worked, Sis.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:16.370
We have enough money to fool around for a while.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:17.480
What are you going to spend it on?

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.920
You're such an idiot.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.840
Money isn't meant for fooling around.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:23.000
Money is used to earn more money.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:23.980
Come on...

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.910
What's wrong, Sis?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:29.100
Well, I had a feeling that someone was watching us...

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:29.980
Please...

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:34.770
Are your senses shot after spending all that time with that Shinsengumi failure?

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:37.320
Oh, sorry.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:39.270
Watch where you're going, fool!

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:40.440
Are you okay, Sis?

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:41.760
I'm so sorry.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.310
I'm in a hurry to get to the festival.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.960
<b>Anpan</b>

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:43.950
Festival?

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.290
Where is this festival, eh?

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:51.130
Right here. The Yamazaki Spring Bread Festival.

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:00.390
Day 63 of the Yamazaki Bread Festival.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:07.080
Y-You really like anpan, huh...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.770
I don't.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.770
And so, I once again munch on anpan.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.190
Sure.

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:19.080
I happen to be a fan of baseball.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:21.860
I'd be happy to accompany you.

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:23.140
I knew it...

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.920
You don't want to come with me.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.720
Um, I said that I'd be happy to accompany you.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.910
Of course...

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:30.430
Happy to accompany me...

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:32.400
Happy?

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:33.930
Huh? What'd you just say?

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.300
I said that I'd be happy to watch the baseball game with you.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:38.470
Ho... Ho...

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:41.270
Home run!

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:42.940
Um, you destroyed the tickets.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:48.820
<b>We Are All Warriors in the Battle Against Fate</b>

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:53.070
A true man isn't measured by high education, high income, or height.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.930
The three Hs mean nothing.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:58.310
The only H you need is the H for the hair on your ass.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:04.380
One ass hair and constant persistence is all it takes to penetrate that giant wall.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:08.780
Well, you girly men probably wouldn't understand.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:11.130
He's not really girly, he just eats shit.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:12.680
Shut your trap, you sick bastard.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.860
This must be a trap.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.920
As a fellow sadist, I can guess what's in her mind.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:18.950
Shut up!

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.770
Don't let jealousy cloud your judgment, Benny, 'kay?

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:21.640
BENNIE K?

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:22.730
I don't listen to them.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:26.910
The rain dripping from the roof can carve a hole in stone after enough time!

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:32.610
My relentless rain of love has finally spread open her tightly shut legs!

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:35.400
Your metaphors are too obscene.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:38.050
Did she say anything else?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:38.980
No.

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:42.110
She'll be waiting in front of the station at one on Sunday.

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:45.020
And she told me to stop following her around after this.

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:47.270
And to never visit her business again.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:49.690
Well, we'll be in a relationship now.

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:51.660
So that won't be needed anymore.

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:56.910
Isn't she telling you to completely forget about her after indulging you one last time?

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:58.850
Shut up!  'Kay, Hayashiya?

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.180
His name is Pa Hayashiya.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:03.460
If this is the last time, I won't get another chance!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.290
I will make her mine!

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:11.570
I'll hit a walk-off home run and lead Otae-san back to the bench!

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.840
We're right in the path of the typhoon.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.890
She's not gonna show.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.910
Guess you're out of luck.

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:21.470
It's a little early,

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:25.350
but a gentleman is supposed to arrive early and wait for the lady.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:26.460
Kondo-san...

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.560
Don't worry.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.640
The weather will improve.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.940
Whether it's raining cats or dogs or spears,

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:37.200
my rain of love will never falter!

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.170
There's something lodged in your arm.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:41.720
Huh?!

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:42.700
It's terrible!

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.750
A cargo plane is on fire!

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.030
Part of its load is falling towards Edo!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:46.990
Oh.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:47.920
Don't worry about it.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.030
It's gonna drop right here.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.490
It really is raining spears!

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:53.440
How bad is my luck?!

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.550
I'm like a sponge for bad luck!

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.700
The tickets!

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:02.080
Wait!

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:05.430
It's not safe to run out into the street!

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.290
S-Sorry...

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:08.490
I'm fine.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:10.420
Uh, you're bleeding.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:13.240
I haven't even made it fifty meters,

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:15.920
and I've already experienced fifty years worth of bad luck.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:18.810
Damn it, I'm going on this date!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.520
First, I need the tickets...

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.600
Check it out.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.240
Aren't these tickets for the game today?

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.210
Awesome!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.580
We don't have enough to play baseball because of the typhoon.

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:27.520
Let's go watch the game!

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.100
Excuse me, kids.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.600
Could you let me see those tickets?

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.970
What do you want, old timer?

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:33.750
Huh?

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.340
Whoa, you're covered in blood!

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:38.280
Actually, I just dropped my tickets.

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:40.780
They're probably the ones you're holding.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.710
Could you return them?

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.180
What?

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:44.680
You got any proof?

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:45.720
Okay.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:48.840
Then I'll give you something better in return.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.820
Is there anything you want?

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:53.330
Hm, we have nothing to do because of the typhoon.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.500
Play baseball with us in the gym!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:57.950
S-Sure thing.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.230
I still have time.

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:01.000
And it's just a bunch of kids.

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:08.190
Kagura's pitches are always so thrilling!

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.010
Old timer!

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:11.540
The catcher is supposed to catch the ball!

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.050
R-Right...

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:15.480
I-I need to get going soon...

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:16.520
What's that?!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.220
Don't you want these tickets?

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:19.120
Okay!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.240
Let me throw the ball next.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.200
Anything but battery mates with the China girl.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.090
Okay.

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:26.750
Here it comes.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.030
See ya, old timer!

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:33.550
Let's do this again sometime!

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:36.540
<b>Beetle King - Throwaway Matches
Kind of serious contest!
There will be kind of serious battles now!</b>

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:36.950
Let us know which match was obviously thrown!

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:39.670
This isn't just bad luck!

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:43.090
I'm bruised all over, and it was just a waste of time?!

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:46.690
Some evil force is actively interfering with my love!

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.050
Oh, you found something nice there.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:51.230
You should go with your brother.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.940
Doesn't he like baseball?

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:55.060
I don't know if he'll come.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:57.530
He hasn't left his room ever since...

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:58.310
Wait!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:16:59.730
Where did you find those tickets, China girl?!

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:00.710
I didn't find them.

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:01.530
Sachiko-chan did.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:02.270
Sachiko-chan!

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.800
Those belong to me!

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:06.170
I'll be in a lot of trouble without them!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.240
Really?

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:11.210
I thought they were a gift from God.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.410
It's too bad.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.150
Make sure you don't drop them again.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.680
Th-Thank you...

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:18.380
Are you sure?

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:21.450
This could be a chance to get your brother to go outside!

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.360
Ah, it's okay.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:27.920
Anything baseball would be like salt on an old wound.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:31.400
My brother used to love baseball so much.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.780
He would always play catch with our father by the river.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.680
I loved to watch them.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:42.900
But one day, my brother threw the ball too high,

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:45.360
and our father went after it.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:46.850
He hasn't...

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:49.910
...come home since.

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:56.060
How far did our father go chasing after it?

00:17:57.180 --> 00:18:02.820
My brother's been waiting for him to come back with the ball.

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:04.590
Sachiko-chan!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.500
Are you sure?

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.070
Are you really sure about this?

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:13.600
What would you know?!

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.310
Brother!

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:16.510
Y-Yes...

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.400
That's right...

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:21.180
Stop throwing balls into the past.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:24.670
Baseballs are meant to be thrown forward!

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:28.530
I could feel your ball touch my heart!

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:31.060
I'm sure your old man felt the same way!

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:34.080
Thank you for helping my brother come outside!

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:35.750
Nice job, gorilla!

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:37.040
I'm going to use my full strength!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:37.740
Huh?

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:40.360
I want you to feel my true strength!

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:41.590
Wait, wait, wait...

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:42.400
Here I go!

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:45.090
Wait a second!

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:48.280
Thank you very much!

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:50.720
Why is everyone interfering with my love?

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:56.400
It's like the heavens are trying to keep me away from Otae-san!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.230
But I refuse to give up!

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:00.190
I can still hit a walk-off home run!

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:01.510
You found our father?!

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:03.010
Wasn't he dead?

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.320
He's lost his memory?!

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.080
Is there anything you can do?!

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.130
Something to help him remember?

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:10.310
There isn't anything to...

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:15.700
What is this burning passion in my chest?!

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:16.940
Father!

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.710
Your memory's back!

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:19.630
Yeah.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.470
I remembered everything by playing catch.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.160
Father!

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:27.320
I don't know who you are, but thank you very much.

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:28.830
Is there any way to thank you?

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:30.050
No, it's okay.

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:33.640
Anyway, you've finally been reunited.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:37.460
The three of you should go enjoy the game.

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.040
Those are...

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:40.170
It's okay.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:42.440
Have fun in my place.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.610
Thank you very much!

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:46.200
We'll return the favor one day!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.580
Are you sure?

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.670
Yeah, I'm already late.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:55.330
I guess that Otae-san and I aren't meant to be together in this lifetime.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:20:01.470
Fate has chosen to stand in our way, and there's nothing I can do about it.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:05.690
As I watched the skies clear the moment I relinquished the tickets,

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:07.630
that was the conclusion I reached.

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.960
I wonder if Otae-san is waiting for me.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:12.880
Of course not.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:16.490
Kondo-san.

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:17.260
Toshi?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:19.500
Sorry it's not your girl.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:21.690
Heh, the girl doesn't matter anymore.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:24.470
I'm devoting myself to the sword.

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:25.770
I see.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.420
Sorry to bother you while you're down,

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:29.100
but we have a problem on our hands.

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:31.050
A meteorite is approaching Edo.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:31.940
Huh?

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:33.220
It's nothing serious.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:35.060
The meteorite's the size of a baseball.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:38.670
It's so small that they couldn't detect it until now,

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:41.520
but at this rate, it's going to hit your date spot in 15 minutes.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:42.960
What?!

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:45.910
We'll have to issue an evacuation order.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:48.540
Well, there probably won't be much damage,

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:51.080
but you better stay away from the dome.

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.290
Huh?

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.530
Kondo-san?

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.760
Kondo-san?!

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:56.220
I just know it!

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:59.220
The meteorite is headed right for Otae-san!

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:04.190
Because I was trying to defy fate and make Otae-san mine,

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:08.110
fate is going after Otae-san now!

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:11.240
Hey!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:12.640
Here it comes!

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:14.420
It's coming this way!

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:15.850
Huh?

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:17.370
Is it coming...

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:18.830
...for me?

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:20.540
No.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:24.880
Kondo will pinch hit for you.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.330
Kondo-san...

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:27.740
Mister!

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:29.620
We've got you covered!

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:32.610
I'll catch it if you miss!

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:36.190
It's over, fate.

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:39.260
I'm not interested in going to heaven.

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:42.220
I live for love...

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:45.410
To protect my loved ones...

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:50.060
I live as a samurai!

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:55.610
Here's a walk-off home run!

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:07.690
I'm walking off.

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:45.310
<b>Next Episode
Meals Should Be Balanced</b>

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:41.260
<b>Next time:</b>

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:43.540
<b>It's too confusing when talking about the poster girl for a poster store,</b>

00:23:43.550 --> 00:23:44.980
<b>so call her a sandwich board</b>
